WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.189
I couldn't come out with the song like this
as a brand-new artist.

00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:05.109
I kind of had to Taylor Swift it.

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:11.380
But originally 2006 when she put out "My Song",
it was very approachable and it could be applied

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.300
to a lot of situations.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.140
And I took that same approach.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.369
I'm only one call away.

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:22.490
I'm going to get as many fucking fans as I
can and I'm going to get their mothers to

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:24.519
like the music too, and maybe their dads,
even.

00:00:24.519 --> 00:00:27.019
And then the whole family's going to listen
to my shit.

00:00:27.019 --> 00:00:30.600
It's like bright and happy and everyone has
their iPhones in the air and they're all singing

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.130
along, and now we're on the 'This is about
me' music.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.900
This is what I wanted to say for a long time.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:51.120
When I came up with the song originally, I
was on this hotel bed in this really cool

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.170
room in the Philippines.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:01:00.910
I think back about the time when I was in
that hotel room and she was literally crying

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.920
to me about how mistreated she was by her
ex.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.249
Had me thinking that I could be the guy who
could fix her.

00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:10.229
Like, girls are crazy.

00:01:10.229 --> 00:01:12.530
They're amazing and crazy at the same time.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:19.310
It almost paints a picture of the background
music played at all the parties I went to

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.310
with her.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:25.130
Like a soft kick with noise under it.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.840
I don’t know.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.780
Something people can walk to.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.740
It's a very small industry, this music industry,
so you hear from many different outlets and

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.560
people about, "Oh she's saying this about
you.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:48.280
She told this person that you were shit and
you're no good."

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.140
And I never heard it from the horse's mouth,
so I always thought it would be interesting

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.450
to include that, like, right off the get-go.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:59.880
I have a very Swedish approach to lyrics,
so sometimes my initial scratched lyrics make

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.439
no sense.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.020
As long as the syllables sound good.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:23.040
A typical L.A. party is full of dudes who
look like they took six hours to figure out

00:02:23.049 --> 00:02:25.730
what kind of bomber they were going to wear.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:30.510
Whereas I just walk in with a shirt on that
I've been wearing for two days, because I

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:34.489
wrote a good song in that shirt and I want
to write a good song two days later, so I

00:02:34.489 --> 00:02:37.880
thought it would be a good idea to keep that
shirt on, so I kept the same shirt on and

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:43.540
they're like, "Who is this kid with this half
eyebrow coming into my rented house with my

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.010
rented Audi in the front?"

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.540
It's like that type of shit.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:59.800
I go into the Edition hotel and she's wearing
this very distinct perfume.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:06.730
It's almost like she wore it on purpose, because
it's the perfume that she wore when I first

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:11.299
fell in love with her and I've never fallen
in love with anybody like that before.

00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:19.349
So I came in with someone who, you know, I
was definitely having a nice time with.

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:24.960
I enjoyed her company, but she wore that perfume
on purpose to fuck me up.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.300
Literally, when I saw her I just...

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:41.450
It sounds mean, but I just ditched the girl
that I was with and I was so enamored by this

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.140
girl that I wanted everything...

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:47.219
I knew it was over, but I just thought if
I walked up to her, something would ignite

00:03:47.219 --> 00:03:48.219
again.

00:03:48.219 --> 00:03:50.530
But, I figured she's not coming home with
me tonight.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.200
She just wants attention.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:17.120
We would be talking in the hotel and she would
be like, "Do you want to sleep over?"

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.260
And I'd be like, 'Yes!

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.109
I'm gonna get it in!'

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:21.890
And then nothing would happen.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:27.520
Which is totally fine, but after the fifth
time of that happening, I knew what she was

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.930
doing.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:35.169
I knew that she was trying to make me so embedded
to her that I would never leave her.

00:04:35.169 --> 00:04:38.569
But I would never get what I wanted out of
her.

00:04:38.569 --> 00:04:43.410
So she was just doing that repetitively, just
to get something out of me, which was for

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.700
me to be attached to her hip at all times.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.040
It might've been the first time that

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.419
I kissed her or something simple like that.

00:05:08.419 --> 00:05:16.620
I just kind of in the most manly way possible,
shed a little tear, because it was a lot and

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.210
I didn't expect it to be a lot, either.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.310
It's a real thing, it's not an act.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.180
It's hard to listen to it.

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:28.500
This new music is genuinely me and kind of
minor and dark and I'm not always happy Charlie

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.300
like I appear to be in interviews.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:34.840
I'm crazy, I have perfect pitch, and I hear
car horns and I have to leave the party, because

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.090
I heard too many car horns.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:40.310
And this girl's hitting on me and it stresses
me out that I keep hearing the car horns and

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.970
I'm thinking about a song that I made a couple
of hours ago and I'm comparing it to the key

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:48.690
of the car horn, which is two notes together
rubbing up against each other and it's stressing

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:49.690
me out.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:54.030
And she's getting me a drink and it's too
much to handle, so I have to go home and write

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:55.030
a sad song.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:56.180
This is what this album is about.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.020
This is what this new music is about.

